Subject: [PATCH] Correct low-precision gated-delta parity and support head256
 attention

Native preparation rounding and derivative ordering amplified through the BF16
Qwen3.5 model, exceeding the pre-set adapter-gradient contract. Preserve the
reference GPU operation order for FP16/BF16/autocast full contractions and scan;
keep standalone native preparation and non-autocast FP32. Add tests for the
precision policy and retain unchanged tolerances.

Extend scalar tiled attention to256 with tile16 above128. BF16 training at
these widths uses a math forward result plus native tiled backward and LSE scan
to bound model drift; forward temporaries remain quadratic, saved state linear.
Other dtypes and inference retain fully tiled execution. Default SDPA unchanged.

